    "notes": [
      "Three connected rooms: west alcove, central nave, east sculpture court.",
      "Long oak slab benches only — no sofas, armchairs, or dining chairs.",
      "Benches run parallel to the wall they address. Alcove bench long axis is Z (faces the west wall). Nave and court benches are rotated 90° so the long axis runs along X (faces the back wall).",
      "Circulation: enter from the open south, cross the stone threshold, pass the stele, then either the west alcove (around the pier or through its portal), the nave aisle around the central bench, or the east court through the wide portal. Sculpture plinths sit off those paths."
    ]
